erated,</em> or <em>cancelled, it; removed,</em> or <em>did away with, its impression</em> or <em>trace.</em> (K.) ― -b2- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">مَحَتِ الرِّيحُ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">عَنْهُ الأَسْقَامَ وَالدُّنُوبَ</span> <em>The wind made to pass away,</em> or <em>dispelled, the clouds.</em> (TA.) ― -b3- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">مَحَا الصُّبْحُ اللَّيلَ</span> <em>Daybreak dispelled the night.</em> (TA.) ― -b4- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">مَحَااللّٰهُ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">عَنْهُ الأَسْقَامَ وَالدُّنُوبَ</span> [<em>God removed from him diseases and sins;</em> as though He cancelled them]. (Msb in art. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">عفو</span>.) ― -b5- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">الاِحْسَانُ يَمْحُو الاِسَاءَةَ</span> <em>Beneficence effaces, obliterates,</em> or <em>cancels, evil conduct.</em> (TA) </div>","pages":null,"shownPages":null,"chars":2772,"entries":10,"shownEntries":10,"truncated":false,"match":"direct","key":"mHw"}